# trials.jsonl — research-program trials ledger (PH-STRAT-002 P00).
# One JSON object per evaluated hypothesis / parameter sweep. Append-only.
# Schema v1: {v, ts, hypothesis_id, family, n_combos, is_sharpe, verdict, notes}
# Schema v2 (2026-08-25, audit D9) adds: sharpe_footing (MANDATORY enum:
#   per_trade | per_daily | per_bar), estimate (bool: an arithmetic guess, not a
#   measurement), supersedes ([uid,...]: machine-readable correction pointer),
#   rescreen_of (str: a second look at seen data, still a countable trial), and
#   the rule n_combos >= 1. v1 lines still load; the loader defaults their
#   footing to per_daily (the contract the v1 header below declared).
# is_sharpe = PER-OBSERVATION Sharpe on `sharpe_footing`, NOT annualized. Most
# backfilled values are approximate (historical annualized / sqrt(252)) and are
# recorded CONSERVATIVELY so the trials-deflated Sharpe (dsr.py) is deliberately
# pessimistic about search. WARNING: that claim was FALSE for D6/D7/D8, whose
# screens were never run — see the v2 correction batch at the end of this file.
# n_combos = configurations actually swept (conservative over-count is safe: it
# only raises the best-of-N chance bar). Feeds trials_ledger.total_trials().
# CORRECTIONS ARE APPENDED, NEVER APPLIED IN PLACE — this is a pre-registration
# artifact and the audit trail is the point.
