{"v":2,"ts":"2026-09-05","hypothesis_id":"XF2_bar_clock_distribution_diagnostic","family":"substrate","n_combos":7,"is_sharpe":null,"sharpe_footing":"per_daily","estimate":false,"verdict":"MEASUREMENT","notes":"SUBSTRATE MEASUREMENT, no alpha selected, no P&L computed, no card exists. Compared return distributions across sampling clocks on DEV 2017-2023 M1 (372,191 rows, 1,537 sessions), intra-segment returns only: M1 time bars; volume bars V*=10k and 20k; dollar bars D*=12M; tick bars; and BAR-COUNT-MATCHED time-bar controls at 15/20/25xM1. RESULT: excess kurtosis 167.05 (M1) -> 5.08 (V*=10k) -> 3.17 (V*=20k); JB/n 1163 -> 1.09 -> 0.42. The matched-count control rules out CLT/aggregation as the explanation: at ~16-23k bars the time-bar controls sit at kurtosis 18-24 vs 5.08 for volume bars. Volatility clustering acf1|r| falls 0.349 -> 0.241 (reduced, not removed). Dollar bars UNDERPERFORM volume bars here (kurt 16.55) at a fixed D*, because trade count rather than notional governs return variance. NO STRATEGY, NO SIGNAL, NO RETURN SERIES WAS SCORED. WHY selects_alpha=false: same argument as XF1 -- no performance statistic was produced. Same operator ratification caveat (ADR 0036 Q1). CONVERTS TO A TRIAL the moment a card is built on a non-M1 clock or a threshold is chosen on evidence.","selects_alpha":false}
