{"v": 2, "ts": "2026-09-06", "hypothesis_id": "C7_entry_deploy_scan", "family": "execution-overlay", "n_combos": 9, "is_sharpe": 0.0043, "sharpe_footing": "per_trade", "estimate": false, "verdict": "KILL", "notes": "Entry-deployment scan over the frozen C7 entries, dev only: time delay (0/5/15/30/60 market minutes) and resting-limit pullback (0/0.1/0.25/0.5 xATR, 60-minute wait). DELAY destroys the edge monotonically from the first step (+0.069 -> -0.039 at 5min -> -0.803 at 15min): the reversal is front-loaded at the D+1 open, consistent with the card's own decomposition (intraday leg +1.086). PULLBACK is worse and instructive: fill_rate 1.00 -> 0.638 at 0.1xATR while net/trade goes +0.069 -> -1.474 and net/event (P&L spread over ALL signals, unfilled=0) goes to -0.940 - the unfilled signals are precisely the winners that ran away. Pullback fills are modelled OPTIMISTICALLY (a touch counts as a fill, no queue), so fill_rate is an upper bound. SELECTS ALPHA: yes. Source: notebooks/10_trade_anatomy.ipynb S10.3-10.4.", "selects_alpha": true}
{"v": 2, "ts": "2026-09-06", "hypothesis_id": "ALLCARDS_execution_overlay_grid", "family": "execution-overlay", "n_combos": 192, "is_sharpe": 0.0161, "sharpe_footing": "per_trade", "estimate": false, "verdict": "KILL", "notes": "The same TP/SL/time grid (48 cells) run over all four cards' frozen entries, dev only. NO card is improved by an engineered exit: lift(best cell - base) = 0.000 (C7), -1.115 (N1), -0.098 (S8), -8.967 (S7); dsr_best <= 0.0161 everywhere. S7's large negative is an artefact of capping the horizon at one session while the card holds ~29 sessions - it measures the cost of a TIME cap, not of barriers. SELECTS ALPHA: yes. Source: execution_lab.grid_all_cards; notebooks/10_trade_anatomy.ipynb S10.5.", "selects_alpha": true}
{"v": 2, "ts": "2026-09-06", "hypothesis_id": "EXEC_leg_shape_and_stop_synthesis", "family": "execution-probe", "n_combos": 1, "is_sharpe": null, "sharpe_footing": "per_trade", "estimate": false, "verdict": "MEASUREMENT", "notes": "EXECUTION PROBE, no alpha selected (ADR 0030 / A15 category: fixes a COST, does not choose a parameter). Decomposes each card by LEG into scheduled (time known in advance -> a resting limit or an auction is available) vs conditional (fired by price/signal -> must cross). Result: N1 is the ONLY card whose both legs are scheduled (ATC->ATO), i.e. the only one where the maker credit is reachable; C7/S8/S7 each carry one conditional leg. Stop synthesis for C7 (venue has NO stop order): R0 booked-at-level +0.069 (what the ledger assumes) / R1 touch+measured taker slip +0.038 / R2 close-confirm + MTL -0.332 / R3 no stop -0.151. R2 < R3, so the stop as implementable by a bar-driven runner is worse than no stop. Which rung is real is an operator choice worth ~0.37 pt/trade (tick monitor ~ R1, on_bar runner ~ R2). Flip-leg lag for S8/S7 measured separately: mean give-up +0.003 (S8 DEV1) and +0.444 (S7 DEV1) - the bar cadence adds DISPERSION (sd 0.84 / 5.76), not mean drag, contradicting the prediction that it would resemble C7's stop penalty. WHY selects_alpha=false: no maximum over performance statistics was taken; every number is a cost or a leg classification. Source: execution_lab.leg_ladder/reprice_scenarios/stop_synthesis_cost/flip_leg_lag; notebooks/10_trade_anatomy.ipynb S11.", "selects_alpha": false}
